# NER Field Reporter — app configuration.
#
# Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable at bundle time. Copy this file to `.env`
# (already git-ignored) and restart `npx expo start` for a change to take effect.

# --- Backend ---
# THE setting that connects this app to the web console.
#
# Leave it unset while developing against a laptop: the app works the backend out from the
# address Expo is serving on, which is that laptop.
#
# Set it to the SAME URL the website uses (routeOptimiserFrontend/.env → VITE_API_BASE_URL)
# whenever the two must share data. Both clients then write to one database, and a report
# filed here shows up in the review queue on the site. Leaving it unset while the site points
# at a deployed backend is precisely what makes the two look unconnected: the phone files
# into a laptop's SQLite file that the deployed console has never seen.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://ner-logistics-backend.onrender.com
